,"h":9.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"NorthArrow":{"frame":1,"style":"Triangle","fill":[255,255,255,255],"outline":[255,255,255,255]}}},{"id":59,"name":"Scale Bar","x":140.0,"y":359.0,"w":44.0,"h":7.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"ScaleBar":{"frame":1,"units":"Kilometers","divisions":2,"style":"Line","color":[255,255,255,255],"fill":[255,255,255,255]}}},{"id":60,"name":"Line","x":14.0,"y":394.0,"w":270.0,"h":0.5,"visible":true,"kind":{"Line":{"color":[42,58,82,255],"width":0.5,"dir":"Horizontal","head":"None"}}},{"id":61,"name":"Text","x":14.0,"y":395.5,"w":270.0,"h":17.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"Datos: IGAC, Atlas de Colombia: río Magdalena (polígonos de San Agustín a Bocas de Ceniza; el tramo de unos 40 km desde la laguna no está en esa capa)\ny zonas hidrográficas del área Magdalena-Cauca; mapa base físico del IGAC; sombreado: Esri World Hillshade. Represas: UPME, con datos de XM. Fichas: Cormagdalena (longitud, Alto Magdalena),\nUNESCO, Ecopetrol, DIMAR y prensa regional, consultados el 2026-11-11. Cómo se hizo: todo en RustGIS web (web.rustgis.app), con cuatro scripts: datos en PBF\ncuantizado, paradas en GeoJSON escrito en el script, marcadores y fichas emergentes, y layouts. Scripts: github.com/jgregoriorincon/30DayMapChallenge-2026\nFotos (Wikimedia Commons; cada una conserva su licencia): 1 Knomrm (CC BY-SA 4.0); 2 Biodiego88 (CC BY 4.0); 3 Guillermo Vasquez (CC BY 2.0); 4 Mfrancoavellaneda (CC BY-SA 4.0);\n5 Crystalarts (CC0); 6 Daniel Uribe Silva: Magangué, cerca de la confluencia, no la confluencia misma (CC BY-SA 4.0); 7 O--o (CC BY 3.0); 8 Moyogo (CC BY-SA 2.5).","size":6.0,"color":[138,151,171,255],"bold":false}}},{"id":62,"name":"Text","x":14.0,"y":413.0,"w":270.0,"h":5.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"#30DayMapChallenge 2026 · Día 13: Interactions · Hecho con RustGIS · rustgis.app","size":8.0,"color":[95,168,232,255],"bold":false,"align":"Right"}}}],"series":null,"next_id":63},{"name":"Day 13","width":297.0,"height":420.0,"elements":[{"id":2,"name":"Rectangle","x":0.0,"y":0.0,"w":297.0,"h":420.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Rectangle":{"fill":[20,32,43,255],"outline":[20,32,43,255],"width":0.0}}},{"id":1,"name":"Map Frame","x":0.0,"y":40.0,"w":192.0,"h":350.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"MapFrame":{"map":"Magdalena","center":{"x":-74.65,"y":6.45},"scale":3150000.0,"shape":"Rectangle","grid":null,"extent_of":null}}},{"id":3,"name":"Text","x":14.0,"y":8.0,"w":270.0,"h":5.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"30DAYMAPCHALLENGE · DAY 13 · INTERACTIONS · COLOMBIA","size":9.0,"color":[95,168,232,255],"bold":false,"letter_spacing":2.5}}},{"id":4,"name":"Text","x":14.0,"y":14.0,"w":270.0,"h":16.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"The Magdalena in eight stops","size":34.0,"color":[255,255,255,255],"bold":true}}},{"id":5,"name":"Text","x":14.0,"y":30.5,"w":270.0,"h":6.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"From the lake where it rises to Bocas de Ceniza: 1,528 km, through a basin that covers 23% of the country","size":11.0,"color":[184,196,214,255],"bold":false}}},{"id":6,"name":"Text","x":198.0,"y":43.0,"w":90.0,"h":4.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"THE JOURNEY","size":8.0,"color":[95,168,232,255],"bold":true,"letter_spacing":2.0}}},{"id":7,"name":"Picture","x":198.0,"y":50.0,"w":42.0,"h":28.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Picture":{"image":""}}},{"id":8,"name":"Circle","x":196.0,"y":48.0,"w":7.0,"h":7.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Ellipse":{"fill":[198,40,40,255],"outline":[255,255,255,255],"width":0.8}}},{"id":9,"name":"Text","x":196.0,"y":49.1,"w":7.0,"h":5.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"1","size":9.0,"color":[255,255,255,255],"bold":true,"align":"Center"}}},{"id":10,"name":"Text","x":243.0,"y":49.5,"w":44.0,"h":5.5,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"Laguna de la Magdalena","size":10.5,"color":[255,255,255,255],"bold":true}}},{"id":11,"name":"Text","x":243.0,"y":55.0,"w":44.0,"h":3.5,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"San Agustín (Huila)","size":7.0,"color":[143,179,217,255],"bold":false}}},{"id":12,"name":"Text","x":243.0,"y":59.5,"w":44.0,"h":20.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"The source, in the Páramo de Las\nPapas (Colombian Massif), inside\nPuracé National Park. Kilometre 0\nof 1,528.","size":8.0,"color":[230,236,245,255],"bold":false}}},{"id":13,"name":"Picture","x":198.0,"y":91.5,"w":42.0,"h":28.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Picture":{"image":""}}},{"id":14,"name":"Circle","x":196.0,"y":89.5,"w":7.0,"h":7.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Ellipse":{"fill":[198,40,40,255],"outline":[255,255,255,255],"width":0.8}}},{"id":15,"name":"Text","x":196.0,"y":90.6,"w":7.0,"h":5.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"2","size":9.0,"color":[255,255,255,255],"bold":true,"align":"Center"}}},{"id":16,"name":"Text","x":243.0,"y":91.0,"w":44.0,"h":5.5,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"Magdalena Strait","size":10.5,"color":[255,255,255,255],"bold":true}}},{"id":17,"name":"Text","x":243.0,"y":96.5,"w":44.0,"h":3.5,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"San Agustín (Huila)","size":7.0,"color":[143,179,217,255],"bold":false}}},{"id":18,"name":"Text","x":243.0,"y":101.0,"w":44.0,"h":20.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"Near San Agustín, the river\nsqueezes between rocks through a\nchannel about 2.2 m wide.","size":8.0,"color":[230,236,245,255],"bold":false}}},{"id":19,"name":"Picture","x":198.0,"y":133.0,"w":42.0,"h":28.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Picture":{"image":""}}},{"id":20,"name":"Circle","x":196.0,"y":131.0,"w":7.0,"h":7.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Ellipse":{"fill":[198,40,40,255],"outline":[255,255,255,255],"width":0.8}}},{"id":21,"name":"Text","x":196.0,"y":132.1,"w":7.0,"h":5.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"3","size":9.0,"color":[255,255,255,255],"bold":true,"align":"Center"}}},{"id":22,"name":"Text","x":243.0,"y":132.5,"w":44.0,"h":5.5,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"Betania and El Quimbo","size":10.5,"color":[255,255,255,255],"bold":true}}},{"id":23,"name":"Text","x":243.0,"y":138.0,"w":44.0,"h":3.5,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"Yaguará and Gigante (Huila)","size":7.0,"color":[143,179,217,255],"bold":false}}},{"id":24,"name":"Text","x":243.0,"y":142.5,"w":44.0,"h":20.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"Two dams in a row: Betania\n(540 MW, since 1987) and El\nQuimbo (400 MW, since 2015).","size":8.0,"color":[230,236,245,255],"bold":false}}},{"id":25,"name":"Picture","x":198.0,"y":174.5,"w":42.0,"h":28.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Picture":{"image":""}}},{"id":26,"name":"Circle","x":196.0,"y":172.5,"w":7.0,"h":7.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Ellipse":{"fill":[198,40,40,255],"outline":[255,255,255,255],"width":0.8}}},{"id":27,"name":"Text","x":196.0,"y":173.6,"w":7.0,"h":5.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"4","size":9.0,"color":[255,255,255,255],"bold":true,"align":"Center"}}},{"id":28,"name":"Text","x":243.0,"y":174.0,"w":44.0,"h":5.5,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"Honda","size":10.5,"color":[255,255,255,255],"bold":true}}},{"id":29,"name":"Text","x":243.0,"y":179.5,"w":44.0,"h":3.5,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"Honda (Tolima)","size":7.0,"color":[143,179,217,255],"bold":false}}},{"id":30,"name":"Text","x":243.0,"y":184.0,"w":44.0,"h":20.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"The Honda rapids split navigation\nin two. The Upper Magdalena ends\nhere: 565 km from the lake, at\n229 m.","size":8.0,"color":[230,236,245,255],"bold":false}}},{"id":31,"name":"Picture","x":198.0,"y":216.0,"w":42.0,"h":28.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Picture":{"image":""}}},{"id":32,"name":"Circle","x":196.0,"y":214.0,"w":7.0,"h":7.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Ellipse":{"fill":[198,40,40,255],"outline":[255,255,255,255],"width":0.8}}},{"id":33,"name":"Text","x":196.0,"y":215.1,"w":7.0,"h":5.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"5","size":9.0,"color":[255,255,255,255],"bold":true,"align":"Center"}}},{"id":34,"name":"Text","x":243.0,"y":215.5,"w":44.0,"h":5.5,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"Barrancabermeja","size":10.5,"color":[255,255,255,255],"bold":true}}},{"id":35,"name":"Text","x":243.0,"y":221.0,"w":44.0,"h":3.5,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"Barrancabermeja (Santander)","size":7.0,"color":[143,179,217,255],"bold":false}}},{"id":36,"name":"Text","x":243.0,"y":225.5,"w":44.0,"h":20.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"The oil port: its refinery, from\n1922, processes about 250,000\nbarrels a day.","size":8.0,"color":[230,236,245,255],"bold":false}}},{"id":37,"name":"Picture","x":198.0,"y":257.5,"w":42.0,"h":28.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Picture":{"image":""}}},{"id":38,"name":"Circle","x":196.0,"y":255.5,"w":7.0,"h":7.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Ellipse":{"fill":[198,40,40,255],"outline":[255,255,255,255],"width":0.8}}},{"id":39,"name":"Text","x":196.0,"y":256.6,"w":7.0,"h":5.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"6","size":9.0,"color":[255,255,255,255],"bold":true,"align":"Center"}}},{"id":40,"name":"Text","x":243.0,"y":257.0,"w":44.0,"h":5.5,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"Confluence with the Cauca","size":10.5,"color":[255,255,255,255],"bold":true}}},{"id":41,"name":"Text","x":243.0,"y":262.5,"w":44.0,"h":3.5,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"Pinillos (Bolívar)","size":7.0,"color":[143,179,217,255],"bold":false}}},{"id":42,"name":"Text","x":243.0,"y":267.0,"w":44.0,"h":20.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"In the Brazo de Loba, near\nPinillos, the Cauca joins the\nMagdalena.","size":8.0,"color":[230,236,245,255],"bold":false}}},{"id":43,"name":"Picture","x":198.0,"y":299.0,"w":42.0,"h":28.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Picture":{"image":""}}},{"id":44,"name":"Circle","x":196.0,"y":297.0,"w":7.0,"h":7.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Ellipse":{"fill":[198,40,40,255],"outline":[255,255,255,255],"width":0.8}}},{"id":45,"name":"Text","x":196.0,"y":298.1,"w":7.0,"h":5.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"7","size":9.0,"color":[255,255,255,255],"bold":true,"align":"Center"}}},{"id":46,"name":"Text","x":243.0,"y":298.5,"w":44.0,"h":5.5,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"Mompox","size":10.5,"color":[255,255,255,255],"bold":true}}},{"id":47,"name":"Text","x":243.0,"y":304.0,"w":44.0,"h":3.5,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"Santa Cruz de Mompox (Bolívar)","size":7.0,"color":[143,179,217,255],"bold":false}}},{"id":48,"name":"Text","x":243.0,"y":308.5,"w":44.0,"h":20.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"The Mompós branch runs past Santa\nCruz de Mompox, a UNESCO World\nHeritage Site since 1995.","size":8.0,"color":[230,236,245,255],"bold":false}}},{"id":49,"name":"Picture","x":198.0,"y":340.5,"w":42.0,"h":28.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Picture":{"image":""}}},{"id":50,"name":"Circle","x":196.0,"y":338.5,"w":7.0,"h":7.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Ellipse":{"fill":[198,40,40,255],"outline":[255,255,255,255],"width":0.8}}},{"id":51,"name":"Text","x":196.0,"y":339.6,"w":7.0,"h":5.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"8","size":9.0,"color":[255,255,255,255],"bold":true,"align":"Center"}}},{"id":52,"name":"Text","x":243.0,"y":340.0,"w":44.0,"h":5.5,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"Bocas de Ceniza","size":10.5,"color":[255,255,255,255],"bold":true}}},{"id":53,"name":"Text","x":243.0,"y":345.5,"w":44.0,"h":3.5,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"Barranquilla (Atlántico)","size":7.0,"color":[143,179,217,255],"bold":false}}},{"id":54,"name":"Text","x":243.0,"y":350.0,"w":44.0,"h":20.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"The mouth, on the Caribbean. Its\nbreakwaters opened on 22 December\n1936.","size":8.0,"color":[230,236,245,255],"bold":false}}},{"id":55,"name":"Rectangle","x":124.0,"y":330.0,"w":64.0,"h":40.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Rectangle":{"fill":[20,32,43,255],"outline":[95,168,232,255],"width":0.6,"radius":1.5}}},{"id":56,"name":"Text","x":128.0,"y":333.0,"w":58.0,"h":4.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"EXPLORE IT YOURSELF","size":8.0,"color":[95,168,232,255],"bold":true,"letter_spacing":1.5}}},{"id":57,"name":"Text","x":128.0,"y":338.5,"w":58.0,"h":18.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"Open the project in web.rustgis.app\n(link in the repository). In Bookmarks,\ngo from stop 1 to 8; click each red\ndot to see its card.","size":8.0,"color":[230,236,245,255],"bold":false}}},{"id":58,"name":"North Arrow","x":128.0,"y":357.0,"w":6.0,"h":9.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"NorthArrow":{"frame":1,"style":"Triangle","fill":[255,255,255,255],"outline":[255,255,255,255]}}},{"id":59,"name":"Scale Bar","x":140.0,"y":359.0,"w":44.0,"h":7.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"ScaleBar":{"frame":1,"units":"Kilometers","divisions":2,"style":"Line","color":[255,255,255,255],"fill":[255,255,255,255]}}},{"id":60,"name":"Line","x":14.0,"y":394.0,"w":270.0,"h":0.5,"visible":true,"kind":{"Line":{"color":[42,58,82,255],"width":0.5,"dir":"Horizontal","head":"None"}}},{"id":61,"name":"Text","x":14.0,"y":395.5,"w":270.0,"h":17.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"Data: IGAC, Atlas of Colombia: Magdalena River (polygons from San Agustín to Bocas de Ceniza; the ~40 km reach from the lake is not in that layer) and\nthe hydrographic zones of the Magdalena-Cauca area; IGAC physical basemap; hillshade: Esri World Hillshade. Dams: UPME, with XM data. Cards: Cormagdalena (length, Upper Magdalena), UNESCO,\nEcopetrol, DIMAR and regional press, accessed 2026-11-11. How it was made: all in RustGIS web (web.rustgis.app), with four scripts: quantized PBF data,\nstops as GeoJSON written in the script, bookmarks and pop-up cards, and layouts. Scripts: github.com/jgregoriorincon/30DayMapChallenge-2026\nPhotos (Wikimedia Commons; each keeps its licence): 1 Knomrm (CC BY-SA 4.0); 2 Biodiego88 (CC BY 4.0); 3 Guillermo Vasquez (CC BY 2.0); 4 Mfrancoavellaneda (CC BY-SA 4.0);\n5 Crystalarts (CC0); 6 Daniel Uribe Silva: Magangué, near the confluence, not the confluence itself (CC BY-SA 4.0); 7 O--o (CC BY 3.0); 8 Moyogo (CC BY-SA 2.5).","size":6.0,"color":[138,151,171,255],"bold":false}}},{"id":62,"name":"Text","x":14.0,"y":413.0,"w":270.0,"h":5.0,"visible":true,"kind":{"Text":{"text":"#30DayMapChallenge 2026 · Day 13: Interactions · Made with RustGIS · rustgis.app","size":8.0,"color":[95,168,232,255],"bold":false,"align":"Right"}}}],"series":null,"next_id":63}],"folders":[],"styles":[],"ramps":[],"tasks":[],"gp_env":{"extent":null,"cell_size":null},"models":[],"workspaces":[],"link_views":false,"jobs":[],"offline_areas":[],"reports":[],"presentations":[],"notebooks":[],"dl_models":[],"shared":[],"data_stores":[]}